  "answer": "Yes, this has been reported before: Windows Terminal crashing the whole window when a tab is dragged. The past tickets give no fix or workaround. In terminal#8683 the crash was often preceded by the wait cursor, and one user said reinstalling stopped it. Another user in terminal#15689 saw it on Windows 11 but not on Windows 10 with the same version. The team asked reporters in these tickets whether Terminal was running elevated or with UAC disabled, and asked for Feedback Hub crash recordings or crash dumps (in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\CrashDumps). Please include this information on your ticket, along with a Feedback Hub submission link made while reproducing the crash. In terminal#15689 the crash dump showed a stowed XAML exception during pointer input handling. Until a fix ships, avoid dragging tabs and reorder them another way, such as by opening tabs in the order you want."
